Third-party data redistributed with shAnalysis (test fixtures)
================================================================

tests/test_data/Wbd_2-120.a_1d12p_4 (DDK3 decorrelation filter)
  Redistributed under its own MIT license from
  github.com/strawpants/GRACE-filter (R. Rietbroek).

tests/test_data/ITSG-Grace2018_* (monthly, daily Kalman, GRACE-FO files)
  ITSG-Grace2018/ITSG-Grace_operational gravity field solutions,
  Institute of Geodesy, Graz University of Technology (TU Graz).
  Included as test fixtures only; data remain the property of TU Graz.

tests/test_data/TN-13_GEOC_GFZ_RL06_3.txt, TN-13_GEOC_{CSR,JPL}_RL06.3.txt
  (note the GFZ file spells the release with an underscore) and
tests/test_data/TN-14_C30_C20_SLR_GSFC.txt
  GRACE/GRACE-FO Technical Notes (geocenter and SLR C20/C30), publicly
  distributed by the providers (GFZ, CSR, JPL, NASA GSFC) via the GFZ
  ISDC. Included as test fixtures only.

tests/test_data/ITSG-Grace2018_n96_2008-04_head12.snx
  Truncated head of an ITSG SINEX file (TU Graz), test fixture only.

tests/test_data/loadLoveNumbers_Gegout97.txt
  Load Love numbers (Gegout 1997 set) from the GROOPS data collection,
  Graz University of Technology / GROOPS developers,
  https://ftp.tugraz.at/pub/ITSG/groops/data/loading/. Test fixture only.

The shAnalysis source code itself is MIT-licensed; see LICENSE.

GravIS test fixtures
--------------------
tests/test_data/GRAVIS-2B_MEAN_n10_trimmed.shm
tests/test_data/GRAVIS-2B_GIA_ICE-6G_D_VM5a_n10_trimmed.shm(.gz)
tests/test_data/gravis_gis_basins.geojson

Derived from the GravIS COST-G RL02 Level-2B auxiliary products and the
Greenland drainage-basin definitions published at https://gravis.gfz.de,
truncated to degree 10 for use as format fixtures. Licensed CC-BY-4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

  Dahle, C., Murboeck, M. (2025): Post-processed GRACE/GRACE-FO
  Geopotential GSM Coefficients COST-G RL02 (Level-2B Product). V. 0001.
  GFZ Data Services. https://doi.org/10.5880/COST-G.GRAVIS_02_L2B

  Dahle, C., Boergens, E., Sasgen, I., Doehne, T., et al. (2025): GravIS:
  mass anomaly products from satellite gravimetry. Earth Syst. Sci. Data,
  17, 611-631. https://doi.org/10.5194/essd-17-611-2025

  GIA model: Peltier, W.R., Argus, D.F., Drummond, R. (2018), ICE-6G_D
  (VM5a). https://doi.org/10.1002/2016JB013844

  Basin definitions follow Sasgen et al. (2012), Earth Planet. Sci.
  Lett., 333-334, 293-303. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.epsl.2012.03.033
